title: >-
  gapbench: Leakage-safe benchmarking of gap handling for annual heat extremes
  and river-temperature trends
abstract: >-
  gapbench is an MIT-licensed Python package for leakage-safe benchmarking of
  gap handling in annual heat-extreme and river-temperature records. It
  provides joint archive-level gap masks, fitting-period and evaluation
  separation, annual recovery and trend scoring, and reproducible command-line
  examples. The repository also contains the associated case study. This
  citation covers software only: observational data from FOEN, GKD Bayern,
  USGS, NASA POWER, LUBW, and other providers are not licensed by it and
  remain subject to each provider's terms. Restricted observations are not
  redistributed.
